# Psi-Pony

**Alignments.** Any, but they tend to anarchist, unprincipled and scrupulous.

Whether Psi-Ponies are a mutation caused by ley line energy, or by the radiation
that flooded the Earth during the Great Cataclysm, or a horse-like creature from
another world, may never be known.

They look very much like an ordinary Palomino - an even coat of gold with a
blond mane and tail - but they are more intelligent than a horse, faster than
most, and psionic. That comes with strong and distinctive personalities and a
somewhat childlike understanding of things.

## Freedom

A Psi-Pony values its freedom above everything and refuses to be imprisoned or
enslaved. Many will lead a would-be captor into the jaws of a predator, into
quicksand, or into hostile natives, to escape or to punish them.

One that befriends a person, though, makes a marvellous friend, partner and
riding animal - bareback, with no bit and no harness.

## Lore

Fourteen to sixteen hands at the shoulder, eight hundred to a thousand pounds,
and a lifespan of sixteen to twenty-four years against ten to fifteen for an
ordinary horse. They are scattered through the New West and southwest Canada,
and there may be as many as half a million of them.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'psi-pony');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
